    "summary": "Allman‑Dead jam fuels high‑energy set with stellar The Other One",
    "blurb": "The show bursts with a fiery Allman Brothers guest segment, highlighted by an expansive The Other One. Not Fade Away, Truckin', and the debut Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo shine, while the first set delivers solid renditions of Stella Blue and Cumberland Blues.",
    "review": "July 16, 1972 at Dillon Stadium finds the Dead riding a wave of pure electric momentum. The first set rolls smoothly through classics – The Promised Land, Sugaree and a heartfelt Stella Blue – before launching into a crisp take on Cumberland Blues that segues into the inaugural performance of Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo. The second set erupts when Allman Brothers guests, led by Dickey Betts, lock in with the band for an extended, call‑and‑response adventure on The Other One, sandwiched between a driving Truckin' and a thunderous drum break. Jerry’s leads are razor‑sharp, trading phrases with Betts, while Phil’s bass pushes forward, anchoring the improvisations despite the mix’s occasional imbalance. Keith’s keyboards sit high in the soundstage, adding texture even when they verge on distortion. The set closes with a rollicking Not Fade Away → Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad → Hey Bo Diddley medley and a jubilant Johnny B. Goode encore that leaves the crowd buzzing.",
